# TypeScript imports — no re-exports

**Golden rule:** import each symbol from the module that **defines** it. A package `index.ts` may barrel **only its own** `./` modules — never another package.

## Where to import (auth stack example)

| You need | Import from | Not from |
| -------- | ----------- | -------- |
| `createAuthClient`, `getSession`, `AuthUser` | `@internal/auth-client` | `@internal/auth-db` |
| `AccountSummary`, `AdminUserRow`, Zod wire schemas | `@internal/auth-db/api-schemas` | `@internal/auth-client` |
| `GUEST_SESSION_RETENTION_DAYS`, cookie prefix | `@internal/auth-db/constants` | `@internal/auth-client` |
| `parseAuthRole`, `AuthRole` | `@internal/auth-db/roles` or `schema` | `@internal/auth-client` |
| `bootstrapAdminEmails` | `alchemy-utils/bootstrap-admin-emails` | a random worker helper |

Same rule for every workspace package: **`packages/db`**, **`alchemy-utils`**, **`auth-worker/*` subpaths**, etc.

## Forbidden

**Route modules, workers, helpers** — no re-exports at all:

```typescript
// ❌
export { bootstrapAdminEmails } from "alchemy-utils/bootstrap-admin-emails";
export { AccountSummary } from "@internal/auth-db/api-schemas";
```

**Package `index.ts`** — no passthrough from other packages (even for “one import surface”):

```typescript
// ❌ packages/auth-client/src/index.ts
export type { AccountSummary } from "@internal/auth-db/api-schemas";
export { GUEST_SESSION_RETENTION_DAYS } from "@internal/auth-db/constants";
```

**Internal implementation files** may `import` from other packages; they must not **`export { … } from "other-package"`** unless that file is not acting as a barrel (prefer not to re-export at all outside `index.ts`).

## Required at call sites

```typescript
import { createAuthClient } from "@internal/auth-client";
import { AccountSummary } from "@internal/auth-db/api-schemas";
import { GUEST_SESSION_RETENTION_DAYS } from "@internal/auth-db/constants";
import { bootstrapAdminEmails } from "alchemy-utils/bootstrap-admin-emails";
```

## Allowed — same-package barrel only

`packages/auth-client/src/index.ts` may re-export **auth-client’s own** modules:

```typescript
// ✅ Re-exports symbols defined under packages/auth-client/src/
export * from "./client";
export * from "./session";
export * from "./constants";
```

`./constants` defines `authApiPrefix`, `AUTH_INTERNAL_ORIGIN`, etc. locally — it may **import** `@internal/auth-db/constants` for `AUTH_SERVICE_BINDING_HOST`, but must not **re-export** auth-db symbols.

## Quick check before adding an export

1. Is the symbol **defined in this file or a sibling `./` module in the same package**? → OK in that package’s `index.ts`.
2. Is it defined in **another package**? → Callers import from that package’s export path; do not add to this package’s index.
